{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--ainu-tripartite-geographic-division","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The Ainu language is primarily divided on geographical grounds into three regional dialect groups: Hokkaido, Sakhalin, and Kuril.","ja":"アイヌ語は地理的基盤に基づき、北海道方言・樺太方言・千島方言の3地域方言群に大別される。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"neutral","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2016@pdftotext-pieces/l0001-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0049-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--asai-1974-dialect-classification","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--asai"],"statement":{"en":"Asai (1974) proposed a classification dividing Ainu into Hokkaido (North, East, Central/South, East/Southeast), Sakhalin (North, Central, South), and Kuril dialect groupings.","ja":"浅井（1974）はアイヌ語を北海道（北・東・中南・東南／東部）、樺太（北・中・南）、千島の各地域方言群に区分する体系を提案した。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu","doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin","doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"neutral","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0104-01","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0046-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--soya-distinct-and-sakhalin-proximate","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--hattori-chiri"],"statement":{"en":"According to Hattori's lexicostatistic analysis, the Sōya dialect is relatively distant from other Hokkaido dialects and is the Hokkaido dialect closest to Sakhalin.","ja":"服部の言語年代学的分析によれば、宗谷方言は他の北海道方言から比較的隔たっており、北海道内で最も樺太方言に近い。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/north/soya","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"neutral","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0103-03","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-09","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-chitose-dialect-belongs-to-a-southern-subgroup","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--asai"],"statement":{"en":"The Chitose dialect belongs to a southern subgroup of the Southwestern Hokkaido Ainu group.","ja":"千歳方言は北海道南西部アイヌ語群の南部下位方言群に属する。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose","doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0129-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--in-asai-s-1974a-cluster-analysis-sakhalin-ainu","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--asai"],"statement":{"en":"In Asai's (1974a) cluster analysis, Sakhalin Ainu branches off first from a combined Hokkaido-Kuril grouping, and within Hokkaido, the Northeast and Eastern Hokkaido group appears closer to Kuril Ainu.","ja":"浅井（1974a）の分析結果では、まず北海道・千島方言と樺太方言との間に大きな差があり、前者がさらに北海道方言と千島方言に分かれ、北海道方言の中でも東北北海道と東部北海道を合わせたグループがより千島方言に近いという結果になっているように見える。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin","doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0104-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-shizunai-dialect-is-representative-of-the-eastern","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--gaps"],"statement":{"en":"The Shizunai dialect is representative of the Eastern dialects of Hokkaido Ainu.","ja":"静内方言は北海道アイヌ語の東部方言を代表する方言である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0044-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-shizunai-dialect-is-situated-on-the-borderline","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--gaps"],"statement":{"en":"The Shizunai dialect is situated on the borderline between southern Hokkaido and eastern Hokkaido, but is reported to be closer to eastern dialects than to southern dialects.","ja":"静内方言は北海道南部と北海道東部の境界に位置するが、その言語は南部の方言よりも東部の方言に近いとされている。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0048-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--according-to-hattori-and-chiri-1960-a-significant","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--hattori-chiri"],"statement":{"en":"According to Hattori and Chiri (1960), a significant statistical gap exists between the Samani dialect and the Niikappu, Piratori, Nukibetsu, and Horobetsu dialects, while Samani shows a closer relationship to the Obihiro and Kushiro dialects.","ja":"服部・知里（1960）によれば、様似方言と新冠・平取・貫気別（・幌別）の方言との間には数字上かなりの断層があり、様似方言はかえって帯広・釧路の方言に対して比較的近い関係を示す。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kushiro"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0103-04","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-basic-vocabulary-of-the-s-ya-dialect","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--hattori-chiri"],"statement":{"en":"The basic vocabulary of the Sōya dialect displays similarities to Sakhalin dialects, but overall the dialect is grouped with eastern Hokkaido Ainu.","ja":"宗谷方言の基礎語彙は樺太方言との類似性を示すが、全体としては北海道東部方言に分類される。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0053-09","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--according-to-hattori-some-hokkaido-dialects-form-subgroups","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--hattori-chiri"],"statement":{"en":"According to Hattori, some Hokkaido dialects form subgroups that are closer to each other, such as Yakumo and Oshamambe; Nukkibetsu, Hiratori, and Niikappu; and Obihiro, Kushiro, and Bihoro.","ja":"服部によれば、北海道方言の中には、八雲と長万部、貫気別・平取・新冠、帯広・釧路・美幌など、互いにより近く下位グループを形成するものがある。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-10","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--according-to-hattori-a-considerable-gap-is-seen","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--hattori-chiri"],"statement":{"en":"According to Hattori, a considerable gap is seen between Samani on the one hand and Niikappu, Hiratori, Nukkibetsu, and Horobetsu on the other.","ja":"服部によれば、様似と新冠・平取・貫気別（および幌別）との間にはかなりの隔たりが見られる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0013-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--according-to-hattori-samani-is-lexicostatistically-rather-close","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--hattori-chiri"],"statement":{"en":"According to Hattori, Samani is lexicostatistically rather close to Obihiro and Kushiro.","ja":"服部によれば、様似は言語年代学的に帯広や釧路とかなり近い。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kushiro","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0013-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--ainu-is-broadly-divided-into-hokkaido-sakhalin-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu is broadly divided into Hokkaido, Sakhalin, and Kuril dialects, with Hokkaido further divided into Northern, Northeastern, Southwestern, and Southeastern subdialects.","ja":"アイヌ語は北海道方言、樺太方言、千島方言に大別され、北海道方言はさらに北部、北東部、南西部、南東部に分かれる。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu","doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin","doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0023-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-hokkaido-dialect-group-is-normally-subdivided-into","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The Hokkaido dialect group is normally subdivided into southern and eastern groupings.","ja":"北海道方言群は通常、南部グループと東部グループに細分される。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-differences-among-hokkaido-dialects-are-said-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The differences among Hokkaido dialects are said to be more phonological and lexical in nature than grammatical.","ja":"北海道諸方言間の差異は、文法的というより音韻的・語彙的な性質のものであると言われている。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0012-07","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-ishikari-dialect-differs-slightly-from-kindaichi-s","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The Ishikari dialect differs slightly from Kindaichi's and Chiri's colloquial grammars, which are based on southern dialects centering around the Hidaka region.","ja":"石狩方言は、日高地方を中心とする南部方言に基づいた金田一や知里の口語文法とわずかに異なる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari","doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--sakhalin-dialects-can-be-roughly-divided-into-east","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--sa-ka-benchmarks"],"statement":{"en":"Sakhalin dialects can be roughly divided into east and west coast groups, and Hokkaido dialects into northeastern and southwestern groups.","ja":"樺太方言はおよそ東海岸と西海岸のグループに、北海道方言は北東部と南西部のグループに区分される。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0002-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--both-hokkaido-and-sakhalin-ainu-can-be-divided","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--sa-ka-benchmarks"],"statement":{"en":"Both Hokkaido and Sakhalin Ainu can be divided into numerous subgroups.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語と樺太アイヌ語はいずれも多数の下位方言群に細分される。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0046-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-saru-and-chitose-dialects-exhibit-a-few","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--saru-chitose-group"],"statement":{"en":"The Saru and Chitose dialects exhibit a few grammatical features that are unrepresentative of Ainu as a whole.","ja":"沙流方言と千歳方言には、アイヌ語全体を代表するとは言いがたい文法特徴がいくつか見られる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:majewicz2022@handbook-epub/l0025-04","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--the-dialects-of-eastern-hidaka-from-shizunai-eastward","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--saru-chitose-group"],"statement":{"en":"The dialects of eastern Hidaka from Shizunai eastward differ in language and customs from western Hidaka including the Saru region.","ja":"静内から東の日高東部地域は、沙流地方を含む日高の西部と言葉も風俗も異なる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0093-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--there-is-a-widely-acknowledged-linguistic-and-cultural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--saru-chitose-group"],"statement":{"en":"There is a widely acknowledged linguistic and cultural divide between eastern Hidaka (Menas un kur) and western Hidaka (Sum un kur), with the boundary drawn roughly between Shizunai and Niikappu.","ja":"日高の東部（Menas un kur）と西部（Sum un kur）の間には言語的・文化的に大きな差があるということは誰もが認めるところであり、その境界線は静内と新冠の境あたりに引けると経験的に一般に認識されている。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["Menas un kur","Sum un kur"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0105-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--eastern-hidaka-dialects-are-not-homogeneous-the-shizunai","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-dialect-classification-and-dialectometry--saru-chitose-group"],"statement":{"en":"Eastern Hidaka dialects are not homogeneous: the Shizunai dialect differs considerably from Urakawa and Samani dialects, and also displays large differences among speakers within Shizunai itself.","ja":"日高東部方言の内部は均質ではなく、特に静内方言は浦河・様似とはかなり違いがあり、さらに静内の中でも話者どうしの差が大きい。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0105-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-10T15-13-12-354Z","status":"grouped"}
